                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Experienced this on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers, had to do Windows 7 compatability fix, otherwise worked fine [/h1]\n\nSo there really isn't much to do in this app.  You explore two rooms in a space ship environment.  One room has the robot avatar characters from the movie.  They each do three lines when you click on them.\n\nThe other room you can look at some objects, listen to tunes from the game soundtrack, and watch a clip of the movie.  The movie clip is decent, but it's a 2D view on a flat screen monitor in a VR environment.  Would have been cool if it had a VR headset attached where you could play the demo (lol!).  \n\nThe real cool thing is one of the objects, that looks like a toaster, has a mirrored bottom.  You can use the reflection to see around the mirror and it's very accurate.  Accurate except when aiming it at the robots, they don't show up.  Are they secretly vampires?  Who knows.\n\nAnyways, the game looks like it will be fun.  Download this app if you're interested in the game, otherwise, it's a waste of your time.",
